1. She misunderstood the meaning of "sure" as sarcastic from a young age, interpreting it as the opposite of agreement. (Verbatim: "I always thought the word sure was a sarcastic word so like if anyone ever said sure I always thought they just meant sure sure okay sure")
2. She believed "brb" meant someone would physically walk away and never return, likening it to a horse's movement. (Verbatim: "I thought when people wrote brb they'd just be like and then and then be like yeah and then they would walk off")
3. She thought "o7" was a fictional chemical formula for "copium," a humorous term for a coping mechanism. (Verbatim: "I thought it was a made-up thing I thought it was a seven turns out it's not")
4. She once thought "pp" meant simply "double p" but later learned it had a different, more adult meaning. (Verbatim: "I have said too much in my life and I will never live that down")
5. As a child, she did not know that raising the middle finger was considered rude and once did so in class without realizing it was offensive. (Verbatim: "I didn't realize that putting up your middle finger was like bad because nobody told me was bad")
6. She grew up in a household where swearing was not taught, and her family did not use profanity. (Verbatim: "my parents don't do it probably because of my nan")
7. Her grandmother, who is over 90, swears frequently and finds it humorous, especially when it comes unexpectedly. (Verbatim: "my nan she's like 90 something okay and and she's just when she swears it's just i don't know why it's just funny")
8. Her father does not swear in general but occasionally swears during road rage incidents. (Verbatim: "my dad won't swear but will swear on his own with road rage")
9. She has a fear of anger and confrontation, often reacting with tears rather than anger. (Verbatim: "I find anger scary I'm one of the i'm the kind of person that instead of angry have you ever been in like an argument... you're just like i'm so eggy i'm so eggy cry cry cry cry cry")
10. She is afraid of driving due to witnessing her grandmother’s traumatic experience with road rage. (Verbatim: "one of the reasons I'm scared to drive is like because of the rage that I've seen") [end of text]



1. She worked at a zoo before becoming a VTuber. (Verbatim: "I worked at the zoo okay but I experienced a lot of issues when I first worked at the zoo...")
2. She has a baby face and is often mistaken for being younger than her actual age. (Verbatim: "I look quite young for my age okay I have like baby face I have baby face...")
3. She was initially assigned to work with children and teenagers due to her appearance, which caused her distress. (Verbatim: "They got me mixed up and thought I was to be put with the children and I was like no I'm here to work...")
4. She found being around school children anxiety-inducing due to past negative experiences in school. (Verbatim: "I didn't have a good time at school so being around actual school children like it's anxiety inducing...")
5. She confronted a manager or HR representative to correct her placement, which led to an emotional confrontation. (Verbatim: "I had to actually confront the manager or like the human resources person to be like hey like I'm in the wrong bit...")
6. She struggled with a manager who was stubborn and refused to acknowledge her correct placement despite evidence. (Verbatim: "She kept like arguing with me and I was like no I literally have like my ID and like the letter and everything...")
7. She cried during the confrontation, despite being angry, due to her people-pleasing nature. (Verbatim: "I was like crying in anger I was like no no no no you're not gonna you're not gonna let me be here...")
8. She eventually stood her ground and successfully transferred to work with animals, specifically giraffes. (Verbatim: "The next day I was hanging out with my school children with the school children and then they opened the door they were like Elliot come with me I'm gonna go work with giraffes...")
9. She has a strong dislike for sparkling water, describing it as "ants with tiny spirits attacking." (Verbatim: "Sparkling water feels like ants with tiny spirits attacking I will never see it any other way anymore...")
10. She used to unfizz fizzy drinks for her younger brother because he couldn't tolerate the carbonation. (Verbatim: "Whenever we had like a fizzy drink I would unfiz it for him and then he could have it...") [end of text]



1. She has a strong affinity for Mary Poppins and considers it a significant childhood influence. (Verbatim: "I watched a lot of Mary Poppins like absolutely tons um mostly because I liked the idea of having magic to clean my room...")
