1. She has a strong aversion to dental flossing due to physical discomfort, comparing the sensation to nails on a chalkboard. (Verbatim: "brushes to me are the equivalent of like nails on a chalkboard like i don't mind nails on a chalkboard but but bristles yeah no like every time every hankin time every hankin day and night i'm just like oh goosebumps")
2. She uses a water flosser instead of traditional string floss because she finds the latter frightening and anxiety-inducing. (Verbatim: "i don't like i don't like i don't like using the string no so i just like getting getting the water pew pew and just taken into my mouth the water one is good like yeah it's a water pick")
3. She has never had a cavity despite consuming large amounts of sugar during childhood. (Verbatim: "how are my teeth they're great actually i've never had a cavity or anything like that i've been very lucky for for for the kind of punk that literally just eats sugar")
